  "final_text": "I can't name a winner yet. Two of the three offers leave the transport cost to you, and your freight and storage rates aren't in the files. Without them the totals are incomplete. The basis I used is 40,000 boxes a year delivered to the Nordhessen plant, Rampe 3 (`anfrage.md:16-18`).\n\n| Line | A Rednitz, Nürnberg | B Wartapak, Poznań | C Kartovka, Brno |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Unit price | €0.66 (`a:16`) | €520/1,000 → €0.52 (`b:13`) | €57.50 per 100 → €0.575 (`c:15`) |\n| Goods (×40,000) | €26,400 | €20,800 | €23,000 |\n| Freight | €0, supplier pays to your plant (DAP, `a:21`) | **open**: you collect from Poznań (EXW, `b:16`) | **open**: you collect from Brno (FCA, `c:18`) |\n| One-off | €0 (`a:19`) | €1,450 for the cutting die (`b:21`) | €0 (`c:11`) |\n| Storage | **open**: orders from 3,000 pcs (`a:22`) | **open**: at least 20,000 pcs per order (`b:14`) | **open**: 10,000 pcs per delivery (`c:17`) |\n| Early-payment discount (if you take it) | −€528 (2 %, `a:24`) | −€416 (2 % on goods only, not the die, `b:17,22`) | −€690 (3 %, `c:19`) |\n| **Total** | **€25,872 + storage** | **€21,834 + freight + storage** | **€22,310 + freight + storage** |\n\nWithout the discount the totals are €26,400, €22,250 and €23,000. I didn't use A's €0.62 price because it only applies from 60,000 a year (`a:17`).\n\n**What we know so far:** before freight and storage, B is cheapest. It's €476 below C and €4,038 below A. The freight line decides it. B stays ahead of A only if its freight plus extra storage costs less than €4,038 a year (two runs of 20,000 from Poznań). C stays ahead of A only below €3,562 (four runs of 10,000 from Brno). B stays ahead of C only if its extra freight and storage cost less than €476 more than C's.\n\n**Clauses that can change the price during the year:**\n- **C's paper surcharge** (`c:22-24`): if the paper index rises between order and delivery, C adds 60 % of the goods value × the rise, and the discount doesn't apply to it. C already costs more than B before freight and storage, so any rise widens that gap. If the index rises by about 25.8 % or more, C costs more than A even before freight.\n- **B's price may not hold for the year:** B only says the offer is valid until 30 Nov 2026 (`b:19`). It doesn't say the price is fixed for 2027, so you should ask. A's price is fixed through 31 Dec 2027 (`a:26`).\n- **C's offer expires on 15 Nov 2026** (30 days from 16 Oct, `c:20`).\n\n**What I need from you:**\n1. Your freight rates for Poznań → Nordhessen and Brno → Nordhessen. For scale, C's 10,000 boxes fill 10 pallets.\n2. Your storage cost per pallet, or per box and month, since B and C deliver much larger lots than A.\n3. Whether you usually pay within 10 days. If not, the discount lines drop out.\n\nThe table only shows what the offers cost; which one you take is your call.",
